{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q583"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1061793204#4_2168816330","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q583","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1061793204#4_2168816330\" , \"end_char\": 4151.000000 , \"headings\": \"U.S. Democracy Has Weakened 'Significantly', Says Freedom House U.S. Democracy Has Weakened 'Significantly', Says Freedom House U.S. Democracy Weakened ‘Significantly’ MORE: READ: \" , \"segment\": \"China, in particular, is actively exporting its approach to internet censorship and <cover>surveillance around the world. In an earlier report, \"Freedom on the Net,\" Freedom House outlined how China </cover>is offering training sessions and study trips, as well as advanced equipment that takes advantage of artificial intelligence and facial recognition technologies, to monitor internet activity. Syria finished last with a score of zero, while Saudi Arabia also finished near the bottom with a score of 7. The report notes progress in some countries. In Angola, Armenia, Ecuador, Ethiopia and Malaysia, leaders responded to growing public demands for democratic progress. The full report from Freedom House can be read here. Tags: United States, democracy, politics, civil rights, world, world news, Sweden, Finland, Norway, Canada, Netherlands, United Kingdom, Greece, Latvia, Croatia, immigration, freedom of speech, Donald Trump, Best Countries"}}
