{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_629400680#5_1383241511","relevance":3,"reason":"This BBC China media profile segment is dedicated to China's media/online environment and directly evidences the scale of censorship: official censorship affects Weibo, the Great Firewall blocks tens of thousands of sites through URL filtering and keyword censoring, and thousands of cyber-police monitor politically and socially sensitive material. It is essentially duplicate evidence from the same BBC article as the prior result.","learned":"Duplicate/confirming evidence: China's Great Firewall blocks tens of thousands of sites via URL and keyword filtering, while thousands of cyber-police monitor and filter sensitive online material."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q601","reason":"The current focused query is producing grade-3 overview sources on the scope and mechanisms of Chinese censorship; continue to see whether additional distinct documents appear."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q601"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_629395272#2_1383226691","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q601","rank":3,"snippet":"limit. The main themes of his leadership have been economic reform to boost market forces, as well as an anti-corruption campaign. Mr Xi rejects Western ideas of constitutional democracy and human rights as models for China, and his government moved to silence voices critical of one-party rule, especially on social media. MEDIA image copyright AFP image caption China has the world's biggest internet audience, but content is tightly controlled China is the largest media market in the world. Outlets operate under tight Communist Party control. The opening-up of the industry has extended to distribution and advertising, but not necessarily to editorial content. Beijing tries to limit access to foreign news by restricting rebroadcasting and the reach of satellite TV, and by blocking websites using an <cover>extensive filtering system known as the \"Great Firewall\". With 772 million users, China </cover>has the world's largest online population. Three powerful companies - Baidu, Alibaba and Tencent - dominate the market.\" , \"start_char\": 1810.000000 , \"title\": \"China country profile - BBC News\" , \"url\": \"http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-asia-pacific-13017877\" }"}}
