{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1436153418#11_2942568711","relevance":3,"reason":"This segment provides direct evidence about the extent and mechanisms of China's internet censorship: popular websites such as Flickr and MySpace are blocked, the system is described as highly sophisticated and effective, about 30,000 censors are involved, companies are required to censor results, criminal laws prohibit politically sensitive publications, and ISPs/internet cafés must record activity. It duplicates the same source judged just before but remains directly relevant.","learned":"Duplicate/confirming evidence: China's censorship system includes large-scale human censorship, platform/search-result censorship requirements, criminal publication restrictions, and monitoring obligations for ISPs and internet cafés."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q617","reason":"The current query is still producing direct, concrete evidence on the scale and mechanisms of Chinese internet censorship; continue while useful results remain and judgment budget allows."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q617"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_795142117#2_1811253692","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q617","rank":6,"snippet":"char\": 1894.000000 , \"headings\": \"33 Amazing Internet Censorship Statistics 33 Amazing Internet Censorship Statistics Internet Censorship Iran Is Ranked As The #1 Internet Censor There Isn’t Any Content That Is Safe How Do People Feel About Internet Censorship? How Can Internet Censorship Be Reduced? \" , \"segment\": \"In China, more than 1 in 4 websites that are normally accessible through Google or other search engines is blocked through a four level <cover>filtering process. The number of media websites that are blocked by the Chinese government: 923. 1.72 billion. That’s the number of people that are affected by internet censorship </cover>on any given day. 25.3% of people encounter at least one form of internet censorship while using the internet. In 2012, the United States had 321 removal requests, which put the country in 2nd place overall. Brazil was first with 697 requests in total. The #1 reason why websites are asked to be blocked or removed is because of defamation. Privacy and security is the second most popular reason.\" , \"start_char\": 1181.000000 , \"title\""}}
