{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ china chinese) (+ \"great firewall\" \"internet censorship\") (+ \"blocked websites\" \"blocked sites\") (+ \"google\" \"facebook\" \"twitter\" \"youtube\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1223374330#6_2523009124","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q618","rank":1,"snippet":"Android, Linux, Fire TV, and certain wifi routers. See also: Our guide to using ExpressVPN in China There are free and paid VPNs available but the former are typically too slow, have limited bandwidth, or won’t work in China. However, most reputable paid VPNs will offer unlimited bandwidth, strong security and no data caps. The best VPNs, particularly the ones that allow you to access content that is blocked in China, will offer their services for either a monthly or yearly subscription. Is Youtube legal in China? Even though Youtube is blocked in China, it’s not illegal to watch it. There is no precedent of anyone being charged with a crime for watching <cover>Youtube or using a VPN. China is well aware of the fact that many internet users are accessing blocked websites using VPNs. As such, the country has employed various methods to block VPN access behind its Great Firewall.</cover>\" , \"start_char\": 2000.000000 , \"title\": \"Is Youtube.com blocked in China and how can you access it?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.comparitech.com/privacy-security-tools/blockedinchina/youtube/\" }"}}
